original_long_description:
About The Role:
We are looking for a Marketing Technology Analyst to join the Business Intelligence team. You will focus on driving acquisition sources attribution and performance marketing efficiency by translating data and information into actionable insights for our stakeholders across the globe. You will have a deep understanding of the marketing toolbox &  capabilities and make sure we’re globally aligned on the way we report our performance. You help us understand the reports and guide key stakeholders in their decision-making to optimize performance. 
A person in this role is comfortable with “all hands on deck” environment, eager to solve non-structured problems and thrive in a hustle startup culture.


What You’ll Do:
 - Multi-touch attribution modeling to ensure we are squeezing maximum efficiency from our campaigns;
 - Be responsible for the Marketing tech stack, research and recommend new technologies and approaches;
 - Own the marketing database management strategy that ensures data quality, supports audience segmentation and data hygiene;
 - Be a vocal and proactive partner to your stakeholders. Guide their line of questioning rather than just fulfilling requests. Provide insights and conclusions rather than data outputs;
 - Know where to find the right data to answer a question. Be persistent in ensuring data quality and resourceful in getting data that is not immediately available;
 - Be comfortable outside of your comfort zone - understand always-changing business needs, explore new tech and tools, trace data issues to the source, or find a new way to address an old problem.


What You’ll Need:
 - 3+ years of Marketing/Customer acquisition analytics experience in a fast-growing tech startup;
 - Proven track record of successfully connecting marketing technologies
Expert in marketing analytics, technology and data visualization (GBQ, Adjust, Tableau etc);
 - You understand how to choose an effective marketing split and how to measure the success of each marketing channel;
 - Ability to build relationships and work seamlessly in a global team environment;
 - Strong team player with excellent verbal, written, presentation and interpersonal communication skills;
 - Extreme attention to detail with great data visualization and presentation skills; you love beautiful graphs and slides;
 - Strong execution skills in a cross-functional environment with multiple stakeholders;
 - Humble, helpful and kind but able to say no so you can ruthlessly prioritize;
 - Proactive, and willing to roll with the punches as the company experiences hypergrowth;
 - You’re comfortable working with ambiguity and forging your own path;
 - You deliver results quickly with iteration, instead of waiting for perfection;
 - You love telling stories with data - numbers are key, but a business is built with people.

We offer:
- Flexible working hours;
- Challenging tasks;
- Young, friendly and skilled development team (middle+ level);
- Skilled management;
- Regular team events and activities;
- Abilities to visit conferences, master classes, pass certifications;
- Comfortable office in the city center;
- Tea, coffee, cookies, fruits;
- 20 working days of paid vacation per year.

AMLSafe is a leading non-custodial DeFi wallet focused on compliance and security. We are on the lookout for a dynamic, energetic, and highly motivated Project Manager to join our international team. If you're ready to face new challenges and have a keen interest in the world of cryptocurrency, then this is the perfect opportunity for you!

Our products also include other crypto compliance-oriented products, such as AMLBot, which facilitates AML, KYC, and KYT, in order to protect businesses and regular users from dirty money risks when interacting with CeFi and DeFi projects.
Job Description:
The Project Manager will play a crucial role in handling the app’s day-to-day operations by overseeing all of the activities, including marketing, development, SMM, and sales. The key will be harmonizing those aspects in order to monetize the app’s existing user base. 

Responsibilities:
Conduct a basic product, marketing, and SMM audit to identify any mistakes, discrepancies, and non-functional aspects;
Harmonize the tone of voice and textual descriptions across the app, website, and social media;
Develop and execute a basic marketing & SMM strategy plan;
Along with the sales team, develop and execute a monetization strategy for our existing user base;
Carry out ongoing market research and suggest product enhancements;
Collaborate with related departments, including the technical team, sales, founders, and PR.

Preferred Qualifications:
Knowledge and interest in the cryptocurrency and blockchain sector;
Excellent communication, organizational, and leadership skills;
A desire to manage complex projects and drive them to success;
A self-starter, able to work independently and as part of a team;
Upper-Intermediate level of English.


What We Offer:

The remuneration for this role is fixed at $1000, with additional bonuses +$2000-3000 based on KPIs that will be determined with the successful candidate;
Flexible schedule and ability to work remotely;
Office in Kyiv (business center Gulliver) with a great view;
Professional growth within the company. Both vertically and horizontally within our other products;
Internal webinars and training for personal & professional growth;
Friendly team that is always supportive. Team-building events.

Join our team and help us develop our business on the international scene while growing professionally and personally and increasing your financial wealth. We offer flat hierarchies, open and transparent communication, and a friendly and cooperative atmosphere.

Are you ready to be a part of a dynamic, forward-thinking team and make a significant impact in the crypto world? If so, we would love to hear from you.

Requirements:
- Work with hardware (Dell, SuperMicro, NAS, SAN, RAID 0,1,5,6,10,50,60) and software (Windows, Linux);
- Plan new infrastructure requirements and maintain current infrastructure;
- Configure and maintain internal network (VLAN, L2, L3 routing, Jumbo frame, RIP, OSPF);
- Configure and support VPN (L2TP, IPSEC, PPTP, SSTP, OpenVPN);
- Deploy and support servers on internal and remote cloud infrastructure (Azure, AWS, Dedicated servers);
- Perform AWS, Azure deployments and automation;
- Prepare automation scripts to perform routine tasks (Bash, PowerShell, Python);
- Prepare automation scenarios to perform routine tasks (Ansible or Puppet, Microsoft System Center);
- Create and support virtual environments (HyperV, ESXi, VMware, LXD, Docker);
- Basic level of maintain CI workflows (Jenkins, GitLab CI, TeamCity);
- Administer and support MS TFS, GitLab;

We offer:
— Opportunities to work with the industry-leading partners and customers;
— Friendly experienced colleagues and perfect work equipment;
— Opportunities for career growth and raising professional skills;
— Comfortable offices in the city center;
— Lunches, snacks, and hot drinks available;
— English courses;
— Travel opportunities;
— Decent salary, tax assistance.

Responsibilities:
- Prepare and maintain asset inventory of company resources;
- Create and maintain access matrix to company systems;
- Mitigate security vulnerabilities, apply latest patches to company systems;
- Apply security best practices to software and hardware configurations and systems;
- Support other departments to troubleshoot technical issues;
- Collaborate with different engineering Teams across different offices;
- Participate in external projects

Our ideal candidate:

- Understand general relationships of the product with other components of the system;
- Understand the product impact on company's business;
- Knowledge holder about the current product status and plans for its development;
- Understand the product value in the current status, the importance and necessity of its improvements, their value for business and company strategic goals achievement. Based on these criteria, together with Product Manager prioritizes the release backlog;
- Manage the behavior analysis process of product users;
- Responsible for the detailed description of the tasks at the BRD level and the coordination of the acceptance criteria with the development team;
- Advise developers (System Analyst) on the correct implementation of tasks during the work process and available for consultance during the release process;
- Have the right to propose changes for consideration and further coordination with the Project Manager within the sprint and release depending on the business need;
- Responsible for the acceptance of tasks in accordance with agreed and approved documentary requirements;
- Expand and detail BRD and describe detailed use-cases with the help of software.

We are interested in:

- 3+ years of experience in product management within dynamic, agile environments. Consumer-facing product experience or complex platform are preferred;
- Proven ability to collaborate with cross-functional teams like engineering, design, marketing and data science;
- Excellent interpersonal skills with ability to influence leadership and other teams;
- Strong business sense and a real passion for using data to make decisions.

Main goals:

- Improve behavioral and business metrics overtime, starting with a comparison to the current platform;
- Customer needs satisfaction research and control;
- Control and delivery product tasks in time.

Being a member of PMLAB team means:

- Challenging tasks with great opportunity to level up your skills;
- Knowledge sharing atmosphere (you have a chance to be a speaker in our internal meetups);
- 20 working days of paid vacation;
- 100% paid sick leaves;
- Medical insurance;
- Weekly events of a corporate employee’s work-life balance program with culture, arts, soft skills lections;
- Sport competitions (football, PubQuiz, basketball, table tennis, bowling championships every year);
- Individual annual training budget with an opportunity to visit paid conferences, training sessions, workshops etc.;
- Corporate library and subscriptions for Pluralsight and Safari online;
- Unlimited good mood and support!
